a's total today they would  would bring its share of global emission  to three and a half percent Let Us  return to Hannah now in Egypt so this  new funding for the African nations some  questions though over whether the  continent is actually prioritizing  fossil fuels or Renewables  but he wants to do both  um and and the position of countries  like Senegal the gas producing Nation  want to sell gas to Germany and Algeria  the gas producing nation is that we have  to lift our own people out of poverty we  have to give them access to electricity  600 million people on the continent  without access to electricity at the  moment they want to create growth they  want to they want to enjoy all the  benefits of consuming energy that  Western Nations have traditionally and  of course they did it exclusively with  dirty fossil fuels and helped to drive  this crisis at the same time of course  they want to invest in Renewables and  their position is that this is about  Justice why can't we do both things  all right Hannah many thanks indeed  Hannah Thomas Peter  now earlier this year the United States  Congress approved a major climate Bill  directing 370 billion dollars into  renewable energy production and reducing  greenhouse gases it was seen as a major  climate Victory with one of the world's  biggest polluters taking a new Direction  bringing a quick reminder of who the  world's biggest polluters are China is  the world's biggest the rest of the top  five made up by the U.S India Russia and  Japan none of these countries leaders  are in charmel Sheikh today although we  do know that Joe Biden will join the  summit after the U.S midterm election  results the question is though would  defeat for Joe Biden's Democrats in  these elections make it harder for him  to deliver on that climate agenda well  the director of independent Think Tank  e3g's DC office Claire Healy joins me  now good to see you Claire so quick  prediction what you think might happen  in the midterms 